@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@* Lightweight layout for generic, tenant-agnostic public pages (sign-in, registration,
   password reset, support/legal/docs). Deliberately does NOT do KioskLayout's per-branch
   whitelabel-branding fetch - these pages are shown before any branch/tenant is known (or apply
   to every tenant equally), so that async lookup was pure overhead and, worse, a real
   post-first-paint re-render: KioskLayout's fetched branch branding could flip `data-theme` and
   inject color overrides after the page had already painted, and it was always fetching one
   hardcoded demo branch's settings regardless of who was actually visiting. Real per-branch
   branding stays on KioskLayout for the customer-facing screens that are actually reached via a
   specific branch (Kiosk, Customer Display, Feedback entry/page). *@
<div class="public-layout" data-theme="light">
    @Body
</div>

<ToastHost />

<style>
    .public-layout {
        min-height: 100vh;
    }
</style>
